=== AI-OFF CONTRACT ===

ADR-015 invariants touched by this slice and the evidence each remains
upheld:

  I1 default-off
     EVIDENCE: TestRegistry_For_OffMode_ReturnsErrProviderDisabled
               (registry refuses construction when ai_mode='off' even
               if the upstream guard is bypassed).
               TestGuard_OffModeReturns404/ai-provider-health/...
               (the new route returns 404 in off mode).

  I3 baseline intact
     EVIDENCE: F1 introduces only NEW surfaces (provider package +
               health route). No baseline handler, worker, hook, or
               page is replaced. `git diff` outside the allowed-files
               list is empty.

  I4 zero egress in off mode
     EVIDENCE: Adapters do not construct HTTP clients at boot — the
               *http.Client is built only inside Chat / Stream / Embed.
               registry.For() returns ErrProviderDisabled BEFORE any
               adapter is instantiated when mode='off'.

  I5 hidden UI (no AI surfaces visible without opt-in)
     EVIDENCE: ai-provider-health entry has Frontend=[] and UITestIDs=[].
               No SPA route, no UI marker. aigen-generated features.ts
               carries the empty arrays through to TS.

  I6 404 routes (every /api/v1/ai/* returns 404 in off mode)
     EVIDENCE: TestGuard_OffModeReturns404 walks features.IDs() and
               asserts 404 for every Backend route. Subtest output
               above shows the new ai-provider-health route is covered
               (PASS).

  I7 per-feature opt-in (default off)
     EVIDENCE: ai-provider-health.DefaultOn=false in registry.go.
               features.CoverageOK() rejects DefaultOn=true at compile
               time and ran clean in `go vet`.

  I9 provider keys never leak in off mode
     EVIDENCE: TestRegistry_HealthSnapshot_OffMode asserts the
               diagnostic returns (zero ActiveProviderInfo, ErrProviderDisabled).
               The handler also returns 404 (not 503) on
               ErrProviderDisabled — defence in depth.

  I10 type system (every AI route guard.Wrap'd, every wrapped route
       in registry)
     EVIDENCE: `go run ./tools/aivet` PASS — 2 AI route(s),
               2 feature(s) in registry, TS mirror in sync.

  I11 (settings redaction in off mode) — UNCHANGED
     EVIDENCE: F1 does not touch internal/api/settings_handler.go;
               the existing redaction of AIProviderConfig in the
               GET /settings response remains in force.

  I12 (jobs + push gated) — N/A
     EVIDENCE: ai-provider-health has empty JobNames=[] + PushKinds=[].

